From: mscharged-port
Subject: Lower the original nonzero-morph software skin positions natively
Upstream-base: efa6fc84680e48bfdca7e6ac245d8abf333ae617

ShaderSkinMesh::SoftwareSkinModel's nonzero-morph branch is paired-single
assembly: ps_add adds the morph delta to the input position (one rounded single
add per component), then the zero-morph transform runs. The native build already
lowers that transform op-for-op (SkinSoftwarePosition) and stopped explicitly on
nonzero morphs. The captain-intro NIS animates facial morphs, so match loading
reached that stop. SkinSoftwareMorphPosition performs the three adds and reuses
the same transform; original weights, ordering, morph buffer and normals are
unchanged.

diff --git a/include/Game/GL/SkinSoftwareSteps.h b/include/Game/GL/SkinSoftwareSteps.h
--- a/include/Game/GL/SkinSoftwareSteps.h
+++ b/include/Game/GL/SkinSoftwareSteps.h
@@ -20,6 +20,19 @@
     }
 }
 
+// Nonzero-morph branch: ps_add first adds the morph delta (one rounded single
+// add per component; the unused second lane of the z pair is ignored), then
+// the same transform as the zero-morph position runs.
+inline void SkinSoftwareMorphPosition(nlVector3& output, const nlVector3& input,
+    const nlVector3& morph, const nlMatrix4& matrix, float weight)
+{
+    nlVector3 position;
+    position.x = input.x + morph.x;
+    position.y = input.y + morph.y;
+    position.z = input.z + morph.z;
+    SkinSoftwarePosition(output, position, matrix, weight);
+}
